  "body": "Found while surveying #339 and confirmed on main with a scratch test.\n\n**What happens:** the upright rapid law `rapids_vs_fixtures` (law d2) sweeps only the flute disc along the segment, with the strict-dip z rule. The shank, holder and spindle housing are never tested against fixture boxes on an upright rapid. The feed law (c2) and the tilted sweep already read the whole tool stack.\n\n**Repro:**\n- A vertical retract from z 0 to 50, with a holder of r20 starting 50 above the tip, beside a bolt 15 mm off-axis that stands to z 60: no hit is reported.\n- A low rapid traverse past a tall clamp bolt is missed the same way.\n\n**Why P0:** a crash into workholding that the post gate lets through.\n\n**Done means:** both cases report `FixtureHit` naming the band (Shank, Holder, Spindle) and block the post. The strict-dip pins still hold (a retract off the mounting face stays silent), and every existing fixture suite keeps its verdicts.\n\nRelated: #339 (triage there, slice 2 proposes the mesh-level version).",
